# PROJECT BASED
# Reports are confidential attack maps (HANDLING.txt). The default output is ~/.aws-enumerator/reports, and the
# CLI refuses to write inside a git work tree without --allow-in-repo (F-066); these patterns are the backstop.
# Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored "reports" also ignored tests/fixtures/**/reports/.
/reports/
/out/
*.zip
*.age
*.gpg
*.minisig
# Owner's local engagement files and wrappers (never committed): keep real targets in *.local.sh
/tmp
/enum.sh
*.local.sh
# Local Claude Code settings (machine-specific; ignored here, not only in a global ignore file)
.claude/settings.local.json
# Internal review docs (untracked by owner decision 2026-10-15)
/internal-docs/
# Owner notes, never committed (F-066 hazard: one `git add .` or `git add docs/` from a push)
/docs/features.md

